# Bruce Lee: Quest of the Dragon (56550016), Thor. DRAFT by lane.routeprep,
# 2026-09-26, not played. One file: no profile screen appears on the way to
# New Game in pass 1, and New Game does not read a save.
#
# Evidence: pass 1 (0-0-y-1790433159-titleplay-p1-brucelee, Thor), frames in
# its route-frames/ (t = seconds after the route started):
#   111133 t20 Ronin logo; 111153 t40 and 111217 t60 an in-engine attract
#   111223 title "Press START" (after the START at t60)
#   111230 New Game (highlighted) / Load Game / Options / Training Mode
#   111239 after the next press: Player Info (highlighted) / Purchase Moves /
#          Continue -- New Game lands on this menu, not in a level
#   111246 A on it opens the Player Info status screen ("B Return To Menu"),
#          which A never leaves; pass 1 sat there for the rest of the run.
#
# The fix: move the cursor to Continue BEFORE pressing A. Cursor moves are
# left-stick flicks (titleroutes: the D-pad did nothing in two games).
# Nothing past Continue has been seen.
wait 55
shot boot55
wait 5
mark booted
press START                 # [seen 111217->111223] attract -> title
wait 6
shot title
press START                 # [inferred] pass 1 pressed A here and reached the menu; START is the prompt
wait 6
shot main-menu              # expect New Game highlighted [seen 111230]
press A                     # [seen 111230->111239] New Game
wait 8
shot new-game-menu          # expect Player Info highlighted [seen 111239]
axis LY max                 # [inferred] down: Purchase Moves
wait 0.15
axis LY mid
wait 0.6
axis LY max                 # [inferred] down: Continue
wait 0.15
axis LY mid
wait 0.6
shot on-continue            # CHECK: Continue highlighted; if the stick did not move it, try axis HATY max
press A                     # [guess] Continue -> level load / story
wait 10
shot after-continue
mark new-game
# [guess] from here: a story cutscene or loading, then the first stage.
# A only: a START that lands in gameplay pauses it (pass 1's generic rounds
# toggled pause). If a cutscene ignores A, the frames will show it; add
# START there.
repeat 8 {
    press A
    wait 6
    shot skip-a
}
mark gameplay               # [guess] placeholder: move to the first frame with Bruce under control
# A fighter: walk at the enemy and strike (A/X/B/Y are the attacks in this
# genre; which is punch or kick is not known).
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 1
    press X
    wait 0.4
    press A
    wait 0.4
    press Y
    wait 0.4
    axis LY mid
    axis LX max
    wait 1
    press B
    wait 0.4
    axis LX mid
}
